The working vocabulary of The Applied ML Workflow — learn these cold; everything else in the module hangs off them.
- **The applied loop** — frame, data, baseline, evaluate, iterate, ship
- **Baselines first** — why simple models set the bar
- **Train/validation/test splits that survive contact with reality** — Tuning against the test set turns it into a second validation set; touching it once gives the only honest number.
- **Experiment discipline** — seeds, versions, run logs
- **Knowing when to stop tuning** — When further iterations stop moving the validation metric meaningfully, or the gains cost more than they are worth — then ship or reframe.

