The working vocabulary of Feature Engineering — learn these cold; everything else in the module hangs off them.
- **Encoding categoricals** — one-hot, ordinal, target
- **Scaling and its interaction with model families** — Scale features to comparable ranges for distance-based models, and verify the effect on your model family by measuring before and after.
- **Datetime features that respect causality** — A feature computed from events after prediction time will not exist when the model scores live — the model learns the future.
- **Text features without leakage** — Using information derived from the target — or from the future — to build features, producing a fake high score that collapses in production.
