Features beat algorithms most of the time. Hands-on transformations plus the audit that catches target leakage before it becomes a fake 0.99.

Work the procedure below on a real dataset, in order — the sequence is the lesson.
1. **Encoding categoricals: one-hot, ordinal, target** — One-hot (simple, explodes with cardinality), ordinal (compact, invents false order), target encoding (powerful, leaks if not done inside CV folds).
2. **Scaling and its interaction with model families** — Scale features to comparable ranges for distance-based models, and verify the effect on your model family by measuring before and after.
3. **Datetime features that respect causality** — A feature computed from events after prediction time will not exist when the model scores live — the model learns the future.
4. **Text features without leakage** — Using information derived from the target — or from the future — to build features, producing a fake high score that collapses in production.
5. **The leakage audit checklist** — For each feature: when it becomes available vs.
6. **Close the loop** — apply every step above to one real dataset, and write down what you tried, what moved the result, and what you would do next.

