The working vocabulary of Model Evaluation — learn these cold; everything else in the module hangs off them.
- **Choosing the metric that matches the business cost** — Match it to the business cost of each mistake type — the metric is a contract with the stakeholder, not a default.
- **Confusion matrices read properly** — The off-diagonal cells are the story — they show exactly how the model fails.
- **Precision/recall tradeoffs on imbalanced data** — A majority-class predictor scores 99% on 1% positives while learning nothing — precision/recall expose the emptiness.
- **Calibration** — when probabilities must mean something
- **Error analysis by slice, not by average** — Breaking errors down by segment (cohort, region, input type) instead of one average — averages hide the slice where the model fails users.

