The working vocabulary of Ensemble Methods — learn these cold; everything else in the module hangs off them.
- **Bagging and why averaging reduces variance** — Averaging decorrelated models cancels variance; bias is roughly unchanged.
- **Random forests** — the strong default
- **Gradient boosting** — sequential error correction
- **XGBoost parameters that actually matter** — Learning rate (eta), tree depth / min child weight, subsample and column sampling, and the number of rounds with early stopping.
- **Stacking and blending without leakage** — Base-model predictions for the meta-learner must come from out-of-fold predictions — never from models that saw those rows in training.
- **When ensembles are not worth the cost** — When a simple model is within noise of the ensemble on the business metric — then serving cost, latency, and complexity buy nothing.

