The working vocabulary of NumPy and pandas — learn these cold; everything else in the module hangs off them.
- **ndarrays** — shapes, dtypes, indexing
- **Broadcasting and vectorization** — Broadcasting implicitly expands mismatched shapes so operations vectorize — the mechanism behind fast array code; never Python loops over elements.
- **DataFrames** — selection, filtering, assignment
- **Groupby and aggregation** — Selection, filtering, assignment, groupby-aggregation, merges, and missing-data handling — the daily wrangling set.
- **Merges, missing data, tidy principles** — Selection, filtering, assignment, groupby-aggregation, merges, and missing-data handling — the daily wrangling set.

