The working vocabulary of Inference and Serving — learn these cold; everything else in the module hangs off them.
- **Batching and throughput vs latency** — Bigger batches raise throughput but add latency per request — tune to your SLA, not to max throughput.
- **VLLM-class serving at a glance** — Paged attention and continuous batching — far higher serving efficiency than naive implementations.
- **Quantized deployment** — quality checks after compression
- **Caching and request routing** — Caching kills repeat cost; routing sends easy queries to cheap models — both directly cut the per-request bill.
- **Cost modeling per thousand requests** — Tokens in/out × price plus infra overhead, at your real traffic mix — the math that decides viability.

