The working vocabulary of NLP Pipelines — learn these cold; everything else in the module hangs off them.
- **Cleaning decisions: what to normalize, what to keep** — Every normalization choice (casing, punctuation, stopwords) changes what the model can learn — choose deliberately, document always.
- **Tokenization choices and their downstream effects** — Vocabulary, OOV handling, and sequence lengths all shift — a tokenizer change is a pipeline change; re-evaluate everything after it.
- **Chunking long documents for models** — Context windows are finite and attention dilutes over length — chunking with overlap preserves retrievable, answerable units.
- **Language detection and mixed-language text** — Tokenizers and rules assume a language — detect, then route.
- **Pipeline reproducibility for text** — Versioned cleaning rules, tokenizer, and chunking params — text preprocessing is code, and code needs versions.

