The working vocabulary of Retrieval-Augmented Generation — learn these cold; everything else in the module hangs off them.
- **Chunking strategies and their tradeoffs** — Small chunks: precise but context-poor; large chunks: rich but noisy and expensive — overlap and structure (headers) help.
- **Embeddings and vector indexes** — Embed chunks into vectors, index them, and retrieve top-k by similarity — the retrieval substrate of the RAG pipeline.
- **Reranking** — precision on top of recall
- **Citations** — grounding answers in sources
- **RAG failure modes and their fixes** — Irrelevant retrieval → fix chunking/hybrid/rerank; ungrounded answers → enforce citation grounding; stale index → refresh pipeline with versioning.

